WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.884
FedRAMP High is an ongoing operational commitment, not a one-time documentation project.

2
00:00:05.884 --> 00:00:10.240
After authorization support work, the system continues to change.

3
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:20.480
Vulnerabilities are discovered, configurations drift, staff roles change, incidents occur, dependencies evolve, and new features may alter the boundary.

4
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:27.281
Continuous monitoring is the discipline that keeps security posture visible as the live system changes.

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:49.365
Continuous monitoring includes vulnerability management, configuration drift detection, change management, incident reporting expectations at a high level, periodic evidence updates, risk tracking, plans of action and milestones, resilience monitoring, privileged activity review, security metrics, and operational ownership.

6
00:00:49.365 --> 00:00:56.319
The details may evolve, but the principle is durable: risk must be watched, reported, and managed over time.

7
00:00:56.319 --> 00:01:00.751
High-impact operations require stronger attention to resilience.

8
00:01:00.751 --> 00:01:13.360
Teams should understand backup and recovery expectations, dependency failure modes, monitoring coverage, escalation paths, and how critical services continue or recover during disruption.

9
00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:19.550
Resilience does not replace access control, incident response, or vulnerability management.

10
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:25.663
It complements them by reducing the chance that a failure becomes a severe mission disruption.

11
00:01:25.663 --> 00:01:29.102
Continuous monitoring also supports federal trust.

12
00:01:29.102 --> 00:01:40.794
Authorizing officials and agency customers need confidence that the provider can identify problems, communicate risk, remediate weaknesses, and keep control evidence current.

13
00:01:40.794 --> 00:01:47.366
A High baseline raises the stakes for that trust because the consequences of failure are more serious.

14
00:01:47.366 --> 00:01:53.861
The operating model needs to show sustained discipline, not a single successful assessment moment.
